  "budget_rationale": "DTI break-even rule: one extra pixel with expected kernel credit w changes the denominator by exactly 0.2, so a pixel pays iff w > 0.2*DTI (0.0556 at 0.2778). Fitting TP=A*n^gamma to the 60,069->0.2477 / 44,090->0.2600 pair and imposing gamma*TP/n = 0.2*DTI gives break-even budgets of 5,400-26,800 px depending on assumed truth size K, with the DTI surface nearly flat over 13k-45k. 24,000 px sits in that flat region and below the historical champion's pixel count."
